.TH "MCP-SERVER-AHA-AQL" "1" "2026-11-24" "mcp-server-aha-aql 0.13.0" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
mcp-server-aha-aql - MCP server for Aha!
with the query language AQL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql stdio\f[R] [subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]]
[api-key-file=\f[I]PATH\f[R]] [default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]]
[read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql http\f[R] [listen=\f[I]HOST:PORT\f[R]]
[subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]] [default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]]
[read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql query\f[R] query=\f[I]STATEMENT\f[R]
[subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]] [api-key-file=\f[I]PATH\f[R]]
[default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]] [read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql execute\f[R] statement=\f[I]STATEMENT\f[R]
[dry-run=true] [subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]] [api-key-file=\f[I]PATH\f[R]]
[default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]] [read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql \[en]version\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql\f[R] is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server
for the Aha!
product management service.
A language model works with Aha!
through one query language, AQL, and two tools: \f[B]query\f[R] reads
with one SELECT or DESCRIBE statement, and \f[B]execute\f[R] changes one
record with one INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE statement.
The server calls the Aha!
REST API, version 1, at https://\f[I]subdomain\f[R].aha.io/api/v1.
.PP
The first word selects the mode:
.TP
\f[B]stdio\f[R]
MCP over standard input and standard output.
.TP
\f[B]http\f[R]
MCP over HTTP on the endpoint /mcp.
Every request brings its credential in the header \f[B]Aha-Api-Key\f[R],
and without a configured subdomain also the header
\f[B]Aha-Subdomain\f[R].
A request with an \f[B]Origin\f[R] header is refused with status 403.
.TP
\f[B]query\f[R]
Manual mode: one call of the tool query.
The result goes to standard output as one line of JSON; an error goes to
standard error as one line that starts with \[lq]error:\[rq].
.TP
\f[B]execute\f[R]
Manual mode: one call of the tool execute.
With \f[B]dry-run=true\f[R] the statement is checked completely and no
write request is sent.
.PP
A value of \f[B]-\f[R] for \f[B]query\f[R] or \f[B]statement\f[R] reads
the statement from standard input.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
\f[B]query\f[R]
Read from Aha!
with one AQL statement.
Parameter \f[B]query\f[R]: one AQL statement.
Forms: SELECT fields FROM entity [WHERE field = `value' [AND \&...]]
[GROUP BY field] [ORDER BY field [DESC]] [LIMIT n], and DESCRIBE entity.
Entities: products, releases, features, epics, requirements,
initiatives, goals, ideas, comments, users, statuses, me.
.TP
\f[B]execute\f[R]
Change ONE record in Aha!
with one AQL statement.
Parameter \f[B]statement\f[R]: one AQL statement.
Forms: INSERT INTO entity (parent, field, \&...)
VALUES (`parent id', `value', \&...); UPDATE entity SET field = `value',
\&...
WHERE id = `id'; DELETE FROM entity WHERE id = `id'.
Not offered when read-only is true.
Each call in stdio and http mode writes one log line to standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]subdomain=\f[R]\f[I]NAME\f[R]
The account name, the part of the address before .aha.io.
.TP
\f[B]api-key-file=\f[R]\f[I]PATH\f[R]
A file that contains the credential.
Only its owner may read it (chmod 600).
Not accepted in http mode.
.TP
\f[B]default-product=\f[R]\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]
The key, numeric id or name of a product.
Examples in tool descriptions and messages use its key.
.TP
\f[B]read-only=true|false\f[R]
With true the tool execute is not offered.
Default false.
.TP
\f[B]listen=\f[R]\f[I]HOST:PORT\f[R]
The address of the http transport.
Default 127.0.0.1:8080.
A non-loopback address needs a TLS endpoint in front of the server.
.TP
\f[B]dry-run=true|false\f[R]
For execute in manual mode.
Default false.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]version\f[R]
Print the version and the SHA256 of the specification, and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
The server reads these variables and no other.
An option takes precedence over its variable, and the key file over
AHA_API_KEY.
.TP
\f[B]AHA_SUBDOMAIN\f[R]
The setting subdomain.
.TP
\f[B]AHA_API_KEY\f[R]
The credential in stdio and manual mode.
Not read in http mode.
.TP
\f[B]AHA_DEFAULT_PRODUCT\f[R]
The setting default-product.
.TP
\f[B]AHA_READ_ONLY\f[R]
The setting read-only, true or false.
.TP
\f[B]HTTPS_PROXY\f[R], \f[B]https_proxy\f[R], \f[B]NO_PROXY\f[R], \f[B]no_proxy\f[R]
The HTTPS proxy for the connection to Aha!, and the hosts without it.
.TP
\f[B]SSL_CERT_FILE\f[R], \f[B]SSL_CERT_DIR\f[R]
The trust store, on Linux.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Manual mode: the tool returned a result.
stdio and http: normal end.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Manual mode: the statement failed.
http: the address cannot be bound.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
The command line or the configuration is wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
mcp-server-aha-aql query query=\[dq]SELECT id, name, status FROM features WHERE release = \[aq]DEMO-R-3\[aq]\[dq]
mcp-server-aha-aql query query=- < statement.aql
mcp-server-aha-aql execute dry-run=true statement=\[dq]UPDATE features SET status = \[aq]Shipped\[aq] WHERE id = \[aq]DEMO-23\[aq]\[dq]
mcp-server-aha-aql http listen=127.0.0.1:8080 subdomain=mycompany
\f[R]
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]/usr/lib/systemd/system/mcp-server-aha-aql.service\f[R]
The systemd unit for the http mode.
